# Blocking jobs return a result snapshot

`startConcatenation` → block until finished → read getters → `reset` is easy to get wrong (stale `outputPath_`, empty cancel text, starting while `Running`). `runWithProgress` starts the job, shows progress, and emits `runFinished` with a `VideoConcatenationResult` snapshot (`succeeded`, `outputPath`, `errorMessage`). It then `resetToIdle()`. Connect `runFinished` before calling, with a queued connection so the slot can destroy the concatenator.

`resetToIdle` must not delete a successful output file on disk. Do not read getters after `runFinished`; the signal argument is the snapshot.

Guard `start*` if already `Running`. Keep split start / `waitWithProgress(callback)` only when the job must span a later UI step (`pendingConcatenator_` during game setup). That callback does not reset, so getters are valid inside it. Neither path blocks the UI thread.

```cpp
// BAD — getters are live object state, and the wait freezes the window
concatenator->startConcatenation(paths, dir);
if (!concatenator->waitWithProgress(this)) {
  warn(concatenator->errorMessage());
}

// GOOD — snapshot arrives after resetToIdle; the UI thread is not blocked
connect(concatenator, &VideoConcatenator::runFinished, this,
        [this](const VideoConcatenationResult& result) {
          if (!result.succeeded) warn(result.errorMessage);
        },
        Qt::QueuedConnection);
concatenator->runWithProgress(paths, dir, this);
```
